{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/146354-world-war-2-the-cold-war-and-watchmen-syndrome","id":146354,"title":"World War 2, The Cold War and Watchmen Syndrome","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-22T21:43:01-07:00","id":146354,"title":"World War 2, The Cold War and Watchmen Syndrome","content":"For a while i been interested in a trans era game. with my players trying to stop world war 2 from happening (but failing), eventually going all Captain America, fighting axis super villians and scientists, from Hellboy Esque adventures! from more Spionage and indiana jones like, from cthulhu mythos to Wilhem &quot;Deathshead.&quot; Strauss.<br /> then working ou the idea of the cold war on a game, from the trenches of WW2 to now Cloak and dagger, characters facing the KGB, the lines of conspiracy and counter conspiracy, the attempt of assassination on kennedy and such, and finally entering the &quot;Watchmen Syndome.&quot; people actually fearing this heroes, asking them to lay low. the goverment keeping them low key and under retirement founds and such...but i wanted to know, where can i find more information about these kinds of settings within the Trinity Continuum Verse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T21:45:18-07:00","id":146359,"title":"","content":"I believe there was talk of a fan supplement for WWII many, many years ago... However, it failed to materialize. Unfortunately, there is very little material for the period of time between 1945 and 1998.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T23:01:40-07:00","id":146440,"title":"","content":"I'd love to play a game which spans eras, but for me WWII would be less Wolfenstein and more Uber, and then into postwar we'd be looking at the Supergod national arms race. Aberrant really benefits from that kind of tone, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T02:33:47-07:00","id":146521,"title":"","content":"Crowley I had the same problem, the best you can do is create your own background for your campaign like I did. I will re-post it here for you, you can use it if you like it or perhaps you can get inspiration from it, hope it helps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As tensions raised between the different countries and the winds of war were blowing again the different governments of the world started to pay more attention to the strange stories about the inspired. Before they dismissed them as nothing more than ridiculous and exaggerated tales destined to help sell more papers and to entertain the masses with their bizarre and bombastic adventures.<br /> However as their research about them kept going on it showed that these individuals were very real and had indeed powers and capabilities beyond human, so they started to see them as something different: weapons. The different superpowers formed secret agencies with the objective to recruit or capture them by whatever means necessary and if they didn't comply....well...the agents had to make sure that the other side didn't get them. The most compassionate would help them live under government surveillance, the most ruthless would murder or enslave them. The Aeon society did the best it could to stop the proliferation of these superhuman weapons and superscience weaponry but despite their best efforts this new weapons race continued.<br /> These secret agencies fought against each other during the war in order to give their side and edge, taking into account the scale of what was at stake in their battles their conflict became a third front on it's own right. The devastation and damage that these super-individuals brought to the war was mind-blowing, the powers that be became terrified and impressed, reinforcing their belief that these individuals should be contained or eliminated.<br /> The Aeon society wanted to intervene as little as possible seeing just how much destruction their powers brought to the war. They focused instead on humanitarian assistance and fighting against evil inspired on the side of the axis. However seeing the horror of the war and the inaction of their friends was the last straw for Doctor Primoris who had grown more and more disappointed with humanity and the Aeon society. He decided to take the matters into his own hands, he would enforce peace even if that meant conquering the world and ruling as a dictator. Luckily the Aeon society stopped him in time but not without a great cost to their members, after his defeat he disappeared never to be seen again.<br /> After the war the soviet union and the united states redoubled their efforts to capture or eliminate the inspired using the chaos of a devastated world and the paranoia of the 50's. Before they were shown some mercy if they agreed to live quiet lives but seeing how powerful they were that option became invalid, they were simply too dangerous and useful to let them run free. In the process they made sure to erase all evidence of their existence from the public to guarantee that none but themselves could use their abilities and super-science. The rest of inspired and secret organizations went into hiding in an effort to avoid persecution or destruction. Some of them would still act from the shadows and others would simply retire.<br /> Primoris had been very busy, he created a magnificent city in a secret island where his followers, human and inspired, could live and prosper. From there he was working from the shadows to make sure that the superpowers destroyed each other in a nuclear war. Safe in their island from the fallout, they would go out into the world and rebuild it from the ashes of the old. It would be a glorious new era for humanity. However after many fights between Primoris and Maxwell they decided to stop and talk. After a passionate discussion with his best friend, Maxwell managed to convince Primoris to leave the world alone. Primoris conceded since he believed that humanity would destroy itself anyway, he would be there to receive Maxwel with open arms when it happened and then they could rebuild the world together as he always dreamed.<br /> Maxwell ,despite his best efforts to hide his abilities and his involvement during the war, was discovered and persecuted. He didn't want to work for amoral governments and turn the aeon society into a target, so he banished in order to avoid capture, protect the society and to help the inspired disappear so they wouldn't end as pawns in the cold war. As time passed he expanded his operations as much as he could with the help of the of the now secret Aeon society and established a sanctuary network to protect the inspired from the world and the world from the inspired, but no matter how much they hid, they kept coming after them. The more the persecution kept going on the more he understood that as long as there were greedy governments and organizations bent on exploiting their powers the world and the inspired would never be safe.<br /> The situation went bad with the Korean war, grew desperate with the close call of the Cuban missile crisis and went further down to the breaking point with the Vietnam war.The public never knew the horrors and battles between inspired and their creations that took place in those dark days. Under the orders of both the soviet union and the united states the inspired fought, died and designed more and more horrible weapons in a frantic race to outmatch the other side. It was only thanks to the intervention of Maxwell, the Aeon society and even doctor primoris in one occasion that the world wasn't destroyed. (both the 50s, 60s and 70s adventure becomes more like a James bond and espionage type of roleplaying game)<br /> Maxwell decided that there was only one option to end the madness, he was very reticent to intervene in such a direct way but he saw no other exit. Maxwell with the help of the Aeon society and other inspired, both friends and foes alike, planned and directed an all assault all over the globe that destroyed the government agencies that enslaved the inspired. At the same time they further erased any evidence of their existence and their creations from even the most secret vaults. They even erased the memories from several key members in the governments. Last but not least and with great pain they also removed the inspired that didn't agree with the secrecy. By the end of the 70s no one ever knew that the inspired ever existed, humanity would be free to pursue it's own path and the inspired could finally rest in peace...at least till 1998. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 05-23-2014, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T08:51:29-07:00","id":146824,"title":"","content":"Not much official information on the period is an understatement <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The only thing I a saw in the various Aberrant books was a newspaper clipping sidebar from a description of some kind of cache that turned up and Proteus had to go in and seize. The clipping was about a mysterious rescue of a car from a railroad crossing by what had to have been a stalwart sometime in the 1950s or thereabouts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}